/*  Deep copies — a value of any kind copied whole, so it can cross from one thread to another.

    ★ Arenas are per thread, so nothing a task makes may be read where another thread's arena holds
      it. A value that crosses — a message sent through a channel, what a task captured, what a named
      task hands back — is copied onto the heap on one side and into the receiver's own arena on
      the other, then the heap copy is freed: `cufet build`'s channel bridge, kind by kind.

    ★ One family per kind: `ccp_<kind>_copy(v, alloc)` copies into whatever `alloc` hands out,
      `ccp_<kind>_freeheap(v)` frees a heap copy, and three wrappers make the crossing itself —
      `heapenv` (to the heap, in an envelope), `arenacopy` (out of the envelope, into this thread's
      arena) and `freeenv` (the envelope, freed). A kind's family is noted as `copy:<kind>` among
      the generated types, after the families of everything it holds.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    Bind text to copy-family, given (the text kind):
        Return "ccp_{cast c-tag on (kind)}".
    Done.

    /// Whether a kind is copied by assignment alone — it holds no address.
    Bind fact to is-plain-copy, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "number" or kind is "fact" or kind is "bits" or kind is "rabbit".
    Done.

    /// The kinds a value of `kind` holds, whose families its own calls.
    Bind series of text or failure to copied-parts unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        Define parts as a series of text.
        If cast is-plain-copy on (kind) or kind is "text", return parts.
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "":
            Insert cast element-of on (kind) into parts.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        If cast is-map on (kind):
            Insert cast map-key-kind on (kind) into parts.
            Insert cast map-value-kind on (kind) into parts.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        If cast is-record on (kind):
            For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), insert cast part-kind on (part) into parts.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "":
            Define definition as the entry for cast object-of on (kind) in one's objects.
            If definition is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("copying a {kind}")).
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Define field-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Insert field-kind into parts.
            Done.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        If cast is-union on (kind):
            For each inner in cast kind-cases on (kind), insert inner into parts.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        If cast is-voidable on (kind):
            Insert cast voidable-inner on (kind) into parts.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        If cast is-failable on (kind):
            Insert "text" into parts.
            If cast failable-inner on (kind) is not "void", insert cast failable-inner on (kind) into parts.
            Return parts.
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {kind} crossing to another task")).
    Done.

    /// Notes a kind's copy family, and the families of everything it holds.
    Bind void or failure to register-copy unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        Define entry as "copy:{kind}".
        If (the entry for entry in one's unions) is not void, return.
        // Noted before what it holds, so a kind that holds itself stops here.
        In one's unions, the entry for entry becomes true.
        For each part in cast one's copied-parts on (kind) or pass the failure off, repeat:
            Cast one's register-copy on (part) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Insert entry into one's union-order.
    Done.

    /// The kind a `copy:` entry names, or "".
    Bind text to copied-kind, given (the text entry):
        If entry starts with "copy:", return the characters from 6 to the end of entry.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// What copies one value of a kind, as the body of its `copy`.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-copy-body unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        Define type-c as cast c-type on (kind).
        If cast is-plain-copy on (kind), return [(void)a; return v;].
        If kind is "text", return [if (!v) return v; size_t n = strlen(v) + 1; char* r = (char*)a(n); memcpy(r, v, n); return r;].
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "":
            Define element as cast element-of on (kind).
            Define c-language series-copied, given (the term series-c, the c-language axiom held-c, the term element-copy),
                as [if (!v) return v; the series-c* r = (the series-c*)a(sizeof(the series-c)); r->len = v->len; r->cap = v->len; r->home = (a == cufet_arena_alloc ? cufet_arena_here() : NULL); r->data = v->len ? (the held-c*)a((size_t)v->len * sizeof(the held-c)) : NULL; for (int i = 0; i < v->len; i++) r->data[i] = the element-copy(v->data[i], a); return r;].
            Return series-copied on (cast series-c-name on (element), cast c-type on (element), "{cast copy-family on (element)}_copy").
        Done.
        If cast is-map on (kind):
            Define key-kind as cast map-key-kind on (kind).
            Define held as cast map-value-kind on (kind).
            Define c-language map-copied, given (the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom held-c, the term key-copy, the term held-copy),
                as [if (!v) return v; the map-c* r = (the map-c*)a(sizeof(the map-c)); r->len = v->len; r->cap = v->len; r->home = (a == cufet_arena_alloc ? cufet_arena_here() : NULL); r->keys = v->len ? (the key-c*)a((size_t)v->len * sizeof(the key-c)) : NULL; r->vals = v->len ? (the held-c*)a((size_t)v->len * sizeof(the held-c)) : NULL; for (int i = 0; i < v->len; i++) { r->keys[i] = the key-copy(v->keys[i], a); r->vals[i] = the held-copy(v->vals[i], a); } return r;].
            Return map-copied on (cast map-c-name on (kind), cast c-type on (key-kind), cast c-type on (held), "{cast copy-family on (key-kind)}_copy", "{cast copy-family on (held)}_copy").
        Done.
        Define c-language copy-begun, given (the c-language axiom type-c), as [the type-c r = v; (void)a;].
        Define c-language field-copied, given (the c-language axiom body, the term member, the term copier),
            as [the body r.the member = the copier(v.the member, a);].
        Define c-language copy-returned, given (the c-language axiom body), as [the body return r;].
        Define body as copy-begun on (type-c).
        If cast is-record on (kind):
            Define place as 0.
            For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
                Increment place by 1.
                The body becomes field-copied on (body, cast record-member on (part, place), "{cast copy-family on (cast part-kind on (part))}_copy").
            Done.
            Return copy-returned on (body).
        Done.
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "":
            Define definition as the entry for cast object-of on (kind) in one's objects but void is cast listed.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Define field-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                The body becomes field-copied on (body, cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1))), "{cast copy-family on (field-kind)}_copy").
            Done.
            Return copy-returned on (body).
        Done.
        If cast is-union on (kind):
            Define c-language arm-copied, given (the c-language axiom arms, the number place, the term member, the term copier),
                as [the arms case the place: r.the member = the copier(v.the member, a); break;].
            Define arms as cast no-c.
            Define place as 0.
            For each inner in cast kind-cases on (kind), repeat:
                The arms becomes arm-copied on (arms, place, "case_{place}", "{cast copy-family on (inner)}_copy").
                Increment place by 1.
            Done.
            Define c-language union-copied, given (the c-language axiom body, the c-language axiom arms),
                as [the body switch (v.tag) { the arms } return r;].
            Return union-copied on (body, arms).
        Done.
        If cast is-voidable on (kind):
            Define c-language voidable-copied, given (the c-language axiom body, the term copier),
                as [the body if (v.has) r.value = the copier(v.value, a); return r;].
            Return voidable-copied on (body, "{cast copy-family on (cast voidable-inner on (kind))}_copy").
        Done.
        // A failable: its value when it worked, its message and category when it did not — built
        // texts live in the arena of the thread that made them, which may be gone by the time
        // anyone reads them.
        Define value-copy as cast no-c.
        If cast failable-inner on (kind) is not "void":
            Define c-language value-copied, given (the term copier), as [if (v.ok) r.value = the copier(v.value, a); ].
            The value-copy becomes value-copied on ("{cast copy-family on (cast failable-inner on (kind))}_copy").
        Done.
        Define c-language failable-copied, given (the c-language axiom body, the c-language axiom value-copy),
            as [the body the value-copy if (!v.ok) { r.failure.message = ccp_text_copy(v.failure.message, a); r.failure.category = v.failure.category ? ccp_text_copy(v.failure.category, a) : NULL; } return r;].
        Return failable-copied on (body, value-copy).
    Done.

    /// What frees a heap copy of a kind, as the body of its `freeheap`.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-free-body unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-plain-copy on (kind), return [(void)v;].
        If kind is "text", return [free((void*)v);].
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "":
            Define c-language series-freed, given (the term element-free),
                as [if (!v) return; for (int i = 0; i < v->len; i++) the element-free(v->data[i]); free(v->data); free(v);].
            Return series-freed on ("{cast copy-family on (cast element-of on (kind))}_freeheap").
        Done.
        If cast is-map on (kind):
            Define c-language map-freed, given (the term key-free, the term held-free),
                as [if (!v) return; for (int i = 0; i < v->len; i++) { the key-free(v->keys[i]); the held-free(v->vals[i]); } free(v->keys); free(v->vals); free(v);].
            Return map-freed on ("{cast copy-family on (cast map-key-kind on (kind))}_freeheap", "{cast copy-family on (cast map-value-kind on (kind))}_freeheap").
        Done.
        Define c-language field-freed, given (the c-language axiom body, the term freer, the term member),
            as [the body the freer(v.the member);].
        Define body as c-verbatim on ([(void)v;]).
        If cast is-record on (kind):
            Define place as 0.
            For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
                Increment place by 1.
                The body becomes field-freed on (body, "{cast copy-family on (cast part-kind on (part))}_freeheap", cast record-member on (part, place)).
            Done.
            Return body.
        Done.
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "":
            Define definition as the entry for cast object-of on (kind) in one's objects but void is cast listed.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Define field-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                The body becomes field-freed on (body, "{cast copy-family on (field-kind)}_freeheap", cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)))).
            Done.
            Return body.
        Done.
        If cast is-union on (kind):
            Define c-language arm-freed, given (the c-language axiom arms, the number place, the term freer, the term member),
                as [the arms case the place: the freer(v.the member); break;].
            Define arms as cast no-c.
            Define place as 0.
            For each inner in cast kind-cases on (kind), repeat:
                The arms becomes arm-freed on (arms, place, "{cast copy-family on (inner)}_freeheap", "case_{place}").
                Increment place by 1.
            Done.
            Define c-language union-freed, given (the c-language axiom body, the c-language axiom arms),
                as [the body switch (v.tag) { the arms }].
            Return union-freed on (body, arms).
        Done.
        If cast is-voidable on (kind):
            Define c-language voidable-freed, given (the c-language axiom body, the term freer), as [the body if (v.has) the freer(v.value);].
            Return voidable-freed on (body, "{cast copy-family on (cast voidable-inner on (kind))}_freeheap").
        Done.
        Define value-free as cast no-c.
        If cast failable-inner on (kind) is not "void":
            Define c-language value-freed, given (the term freer), as [if (v.ok) the freer(v.value); ].
            The value-free becomes value-freed on ("{cast copy-family on (cast failable-inner on (kind))}_freeheap").
        Done.
        Define c-language failable-freed, given (the c-language axiom body, the c-language axiom value-free),
            as [the body the value-free if (!v.ok) { free((void*)v.failure.message); free((void*)v.failure.category); }].
        Return failable-freed on (body, value-free).
    Done.

    /// Every copy family the program noted, declared first so each may call any other, then each
    /// one's body, then the three wrappers that make a crossing.
    Bind text or failure to c-copy-families unto emitter:
        Define kinds-noted as a series of text.
        For each entry in one's union-order, repeat:
            If cast copied-kind on (entry) is not "", insert cast copied-kind on (entry) into kinds-noted.
        Done.
        If the number of kinds-noted is 0, return "".
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "typedef void* (*cufet_alloc_fn)(size_t);\n" into out.
        For each kind in kinds-noted, repeat:
            Define type-c as cast c-type on (kind).
            Define named as cast copy-family on (kind).
            Insert "static {type-c} {named}_copy({type-c} v, cufet_alloc_fn a);\nstatic void {named}_freeheap({type-c} v);\n" into out.
        Done.
        For each kind in kinds-noted, repeat:
            Define type-c as cast c-type on (kind).
            Define named as cast copy-family on (kind).
            Define c-language named-copy-form, given (the c-language axiom type-c, the term named-copy, the c-language axiom c-copy-body),
                as [static the type-c the named-copy(the type-c v, cufet_alloc_fn a) { the c-copy-body }].
            Insert "{named-copy-form on (type-c, "{named}_copy", cast one's c-copy-body on (kind) or pass the failure off)}\n" into out.
            Define c-language named-freeheap-form, given (the term named-freeheap, the c-language axiom type-c, the c-language axiom c-free-body),
                as [static void the named-freeheap(the type-c v) { the c-free-body }].
            Insert "{named-freeheap-form on ("{named}_freeheap", type-c, cast one's c-free-body on (kind) or pass the failure off)}\n" into out.
            Define c-language named-heapenv-form, given (the term named-heapenv, the c-language axiom type-c, the term named-copy),
                as [static void* the named-heapenv(the type-c v) { void* e = malloc(sizeof(the type-c)); *(the type-c*)e = the named-copy(v, malloc); return e; }].
            Insert "{named-heapenv-form on ("{named}_heapenv", type-c, "{named}_copy")}\n" into out.
            Define c-language named-arenacopy-form, given (the c-language axiom type-c, the term named-arenacopy, the term named-copy),
                as [static the type-c the named-arenacopy(void* e) { return the named-copy(*(the type-c*)e, cufet_arena_alloc); }].
            Insert "{named-arenacopy-form on (type-c, "{named}_arenacopy", "{named}_copy")}\n" into out.
            Define c-language named-freeenv-form, given (the term named-freeenv, the term named-freeheap, the c-language axiom type-c),
                as [static void the named-freeenv(void* e) { the named-freeheap(*(the type-c*)e); free(e); }].
            Insert "{named-freeenv-form on ("{named}_freeenv", "{named}_freeheap", type-c)}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Insert "\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.
Done.
